00:30:45,460 --> 00:30:48,980
is that we wanna be judges but we don't wanna be doers.

453
00:30:50,680 --> 00:30:53,060
We have this little area, again,

454
00:30:53,060 --> 00:30:58,060
that we're squared away in and that's our hobby horse.

455
00:30:59,180 --> 00:31:01,580
Are we tracking this morning?

456
00:31:01,580 --> 00:31:04,120
Because this is where we live.

457
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:06,580
There's some people that just have higher music standards

458
00:31:06,580 --> 00:31:09,840
than other people but it doesn't mean

459
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:13,640
that their standard is the right standard for all people.

460
00:31:15,700 --> 00:31:16,540
Got quiet.

461
00:31:17,580 --> 00:31:18,820
I've said this before.

462
00:31:18,820 --> 00:31:21,620
There's a spectrum with music that's okay.

463
00:31:23,380 --> 00:31:27,400
That's biblically sound music and within that spectrum,

464
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:29,040
there's gonna be preference.

465
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:32,680
There's gonna be something that may be over here

466
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:35,120
versus something over here but it doesn't mean it's bad.

467
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:36,440
It doesn't mean it's evil.

468
00:31:37,560 --> 00:31:38,840
Dress standards.

469
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:40,920
There's some people that have different dress standards

470
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:41,840
than other people.

471
00:31:41,840 --> 00:31:43,920
Listen, the reality is that you say,

472
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:46,800
Pastor, you wear a shirt and tie every single service.

473
00:31:46,800 --> 00:31:48,280
Somebody asked me a couple months ago,

474
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:50,280
do you cut grass in a shirt and tie?

475
00:31:50,280 --> 00:31:51,520
No, if you come here during the week,

476
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:52,960
I got a polo shirt on, amen?

477
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:56,720
I don't have a shirt and tie on every day.

478
00:31:56,760 --> 00:31:59,400
I had one guy criticize me because I don't wear t-shirts.

479
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:01,040
I wear a t-shirt if I go to the gym.

480
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:02,120
That's about it.

481
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:03,520
I'm just not a t-shirt guy.

482
00:32:05,080 --> 00:32:09,400
And he was criticizing me in play, in fun.

483
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:11,080
He's like, you're in your house.

484
00:32:11,080 --> 00:32:12,920
Why do you have a polo on?

485
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:15,920
It's just my wardrobe.

486
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,160
But listen, if somebody doesn't come to church

487
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:21,460
with a shirt and tie on, I'm not judging them.

488
00:32:22,860 --> 00:32:24,460
I've never judged one person.

489
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:30,840
Somebody asked me, what do I wear to the banquet

490
00:32:30,840 --> 00:32:33,000
next Wednesday night, the guy that's speaking?

491
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:35,640
He said, what should I wear?

492
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:36,840
I said, well, I'll be the only guy

493
00:32:36,840 --> 00:32:38,840
with a shirt and tie on and a coat.

494
00:32:38,840 --> 00:32:41,940
I said, he's like, so a coat and just a button down,

495
00:32:41,940 --> 00:32:42,780
is that okay, do you want me to wear a tie?

496
00:32:42,780 --> 00:32:44,920
I was like, no, you don't have to wear a tie, it's fine.

497
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:47,200
I said, a coat and a button down's perfect.

498
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,680
He said, all right, that sounds good.

499
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:50,160
He said, you sure you don't want me to wear a suit and tie?

500
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:51,600
No, no, that's okay, I'll be the only one here

501
00:32:51,600 --> 00:32:53,600
with a suit and tie on Wednesday night.

502
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:54,920
And some people say to me, why?

503
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:56,560
Why do you wear a shirt and tie?

504
00:32:58,200 --> 00:32:59,600
And let me just be transparent,

505
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:04,600
it's almost like putting on a uniform, for me, for me.

506
00:33:05,120 --> 00:33:07,200
I've preached, I preached at a men's meeting,

507
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:09,720
some of you were there at the men's meeting over in Manassas,

508
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:12,160
and the pastor asked me to preach

509
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:14,800
with just some khaki pants and a polo shirt.

510
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:17,440
And I did, but I felt uncomfortable.

511
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:21,320
I just did, it's just not my style.

512
00:33:21,320 --> 00:33:22,160
That's okay.

513
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:25,520
We went up on Thursday to go see Brianna.

514
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:27,440
Brianna, she was playing in the championship

515
00:33:27,440 --> 00:33:29,600
volleyball game after church, and we went up there.

516
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:31,560
And I said, listen, I said, we're gonna go,

517
00:33:31,560 --> 00:33:34,000
they have church on Thursday night.

518
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:34,840
I said, we're gonna go to church,

519
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:36,360
I'll have to wear a shirt and tie.

520
00:33:36,360 --> 00:33:38,680
And she's like, ah, you don't have to worry about it.

521
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:41,200
But I took a shirt and tie and a sports coat with me,

522
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:43,760
because that's just me.

523
00:33:43,760 --> 00:33:45,400
And then at five o'clock, I get a phone call

524
00:33:45,400 --> 00:33:48,520
or a text message saying, hey, can you preach tonight?

525
00:33:48,520 --> 00:33:50,240
I was like, praise God, I have a shirt and tie

526
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:51,200
and a sports coat.

527
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:54,600
So I preached on Thursday night.

528
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:58,160
But what I'm saying is that just because I have

529
00:33:58,160 --> 00:34:01,200
that position doesn't make it right for me

530
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:02,920
to judge everybody else.

531
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:07,400
No, if we have a standard for if you're gonna come up

532
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:09,040
on our platform and you're gonna play,

533
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:12,380
you're gonna sing, and we have a standard, and we do,

534
00:34:12,380 --> 00:34:14,040
that's a different thing.

535
00:34:14,040 --> 00:34:17,080
Listen, I taught the teenagers a couple months ago.

536
00:34:17,080 --> 00:34:19,000
I said, how many of you have something that you play

537
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,720
in a band, a concert, something, several of them?

538
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:23,760
When you go to the concert, is there a certain attire

539
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:25,320
that you're supposed to wear?

540
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:27,360
These are teenagers, I'm not talking about adults,

541
00:34:27,360 --> 00:34:29,600
I'm talking about teenagers.

542
00:34:29,600 --> 00:34:31,320
Teenagers sometimes have it more squared away

543
00:34:31,320 --> 00:34:32,520
than adults do.

544
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:34,120
I'm just being honest.

545
00:34:34,120 --> 00:34:36,640
You get less problems from teenagers sometimes

546
00:34:36,640 --> 00:34:37,920
than you do from adults.

547
00:34:38,860 --> 00:34:40,520
And they said, oh yeah, there's a certain attire

548
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:42,640
you gotta wear if you're gonna play in the concert.

549
00:34:42,640 --> 00:34:44,200
I was like, okay, well, what is it?

550
00:34:44,200 --> 00:34:45,040
They told me.

551
00:34:45,040 --> 00:34:47,380
I was like, so does it make you play your instrument

552
00:34:47,380 --> 00:34:49,840
better because you have a tie on?

553
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:52,040
Does it make me preach better because I have a tie on?

554
00:34:52,040 --> 00:34:53,640
No.

555
00:34:53,640 --> 00:34:55,560
In fact, many of you would talk about how a tie

556
00:34:55,560 --> 00:34:57,160
drives you crazy, and it chokes you,

557
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:59,000
and who invented this thing, right?

558
00:35:00,120 --> 00:35:02,000
But the tie doesn't make you play your instrument

559
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,000
any better.

560
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,800
So I said, okay, so what happens if you show up

561
00:35:04,800 --> 00:35:06,280
for the concert and just say, you know what,

562
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:07,440
I know that's what I'm supposed to wear,

563
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:09,640
but I don't care, I'm just gonna show up like this.

564
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:10,760
Jeans and a T-shirt.

565
00:35:11,980 --> 00:35:13,320
What's gonna happen?

566
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:14,920
Mark, you know what the teenagers told me?

567
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:16,380
They ain't gonna let us play.

568
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:19,640
Really?

569
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:21,320
I mean, they're not gonna let you play?

570
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:22,720
Now, what if your parents go and throw a fit,

571
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:24,720
because that's what some parents would do?

572
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:26,680
Guess what?

573
00:35:27,720 --> 00:35:28,560
Too bad.

574
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:33,480
So we see here, I'm trying to use some practical things

575
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:35,100
because the book is practical,

576
00:35:35,100 --> 00:35:37,520
that listen, we have to be understanding

577
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:41,200
that the problem with judging is that sometimes

578
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:43,960
we judge in an area that we quote unquote

579
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:48,080
have squared away while we leave other areas undone.

580
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:50,040
We say we don't wanna talk about those areas,

581
00:35:50,040 --> 00:35:53,600
we don't wanna have this, and it's problematic.

582
00:35:53,600 --> 00:35:55,960
And it causes division.

583
00:35:55,960 --> 00:36:00,800
It causes contention within the household of faith.

584
00:36:00,800 --> 00:36:05,020
And so we find here, there's this problem with judging.

585
00:36:05,020 --> 00:36:08,720
Again, I've said it twice, I'll say it a final time,

586
00:36:08,720 --> 00:36:12,320
it's not the problem that judging is bad,

587
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:15,580
the problem is that the one that's illustrated here

588
00:36:15,580 --> 00:36:17,740
is judging is not doing.

589
00:36:18,700 --> 00:36:21,980
They're too concerned with judging

590
00:36:21,980 --> 00:36:25,580
and not concerned with personal examination.

591
00:36:25,580 --> 00:36:27,260
And that's the problem.

592
00:36:27,260 --> 00:36:29,900
Notice not only the problem of judging,

593
00:36:29,900 --> 00:36:33,460
but we see number two, the priority of doing.

594
00:36:33,460 --> 00:36:34,600
The priority of doing.

595
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:37,300
Now, this is obvious as we've kind of spent

596
00:36:37,300 --> 00:36:39,580
all of our time, most of our time on the first point

597
00:36:39,580 --> 00:36:42,460
on purpose, and we see this priority of doing.

598
00:36:42,460 --> 00:36:45,520
The theme of the book, the theme for our church,

599
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:47,840
is from James chapter number one.

600
00:36:47,840 --> 00:36:50,880
Look at what it says in James one and verse 22.

601
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:55,120
James one and verse 22.

602
00:36:57,320 --> 00:37:02,280
But be doers of the word and not hearers only.

603
00:37:02,280 --> 00:37:05,120
And then notice the last part of the verse, deceiving who?

604
00:37:06,120 --> 00:37:11,040
Deceiving your own selves.

605
00:37:11,040 --> 00:37:14,520
It's not that you're deceiving someone else,

606
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:16,400
you're deceiving yourself.

607
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:19,200
And so we find, he says in verse 33,

608
00:37:19,200 --> 00:37:21,640
for if any man be a hearer, for if any, excuse me,

609
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:26,120
be a hearer of the word and not a doer,

610
00:37:26,120 --> 00:37:29,080
he is likened to a man beholding his natural face

611
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:32,360
in a glass, for he beholdeth himself and goeth his way

612
00:37:32,360 --> 00:37:37,000
and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was.

613
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:40,840
But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty,

614
00:37:40,840 --> 00:37:44,200
the word of God, and continueth therein,

615
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:46,080
and that's being a doer of the word,

616
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:50,400
he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work,

617
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:54,520
this man shall be blessed in his deed.

618
00:37:55,640 --> 00:37:57,600
I said this as well on Wednesday evening,

619
00:37:57,600 --> 00:38:01,920
the Bible's a big book, 1,189 chapters.

620
00:38:01,920 --> 00:38:03,480
I mean, it's a big book.

621
00:38:04,840 --> 00:38:07,600
I guarantee you that you've read something at some point

622
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:10,840
that you have forgotten from the Bible.

623
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:11,860
I guarantee it.

624
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:17,200
Why do I make that point?

625
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:22,200
Well, because the reality of this priority of doing

626
00:38:23,840 --> 00:38:26,920
is that if I just get really focused

627
00:38:26,920 --> 00:38:29,840
on being a follower of Jesus Christ,

628
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:33,120
and I get really focused about what God wants of me,

629
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:36,880
and what pleases God in my life,

630
00:38:38,040 --> 00:38:39,600
I'm not really gonna have a whole lot of time

631
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:40,720
to judge other people.

632
00:38:41,680 --> 00:38:43,240
Does that make sense?

633
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:44,080
Why?

634
00:38:44,080 --> 00:38:47,280
Because this is a big book, and there's a lot of truth,

635
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:49,840
and I gotta constantly be going back to the word of God

636
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,560
and saying, how do I apply this?

637
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:53,120
What am I supposed to do with this?

638
00:38:53,120 --> 00:38:54,160
What pleases God?

639
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:57,200
Prove, prove what is acceptable unto the Lord.

640
00:38:57,200 --> 00:39:00,000
Prove all things in 1 Thessalonians chapter five,

641
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:02,000
and I'm proving, and I'm working, and I'm studying,

642
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:03,400
and I'm going through the word of God,

643
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:05,720
and I'm seeking to be living a life

644
00:39:05,720 --> 00:39:08,320
that's pleasing to the Lord.

645
00:39:08,320 --> 00:39:11,280
I don't have time to be judging over this one little thing

646
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:13,600
that I think I have squared away in my life,

647
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:16,280
when there's all these other things that are undone.

648
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:18,080
Does that make sense?

649
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:20,720
And so there has to be this priority of doing.

650
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:23,240
Now, understand with me that there should be,

651
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:26,360
there will be a time in which we need

652
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:28,180
to judge righteous judgment.

653
00:39:28,180 --> 00:39:30,800
That's why we built the foundation in our first point

654
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:33,480
of what Jesus said in John chapter seven,

655
00:39:33,480 --> 00:39:36,640
of what Paul said in 1 Corinthians five and six,

656
00:39:36,640 --> 00:39:38,600
and understanding that there might be a time

657
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:42,080
that we do have to judge amongst matters,

658
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:45,920
just as Moses and others did, but that's not my focus.

659
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:47,440
That's not my priority.

660
00:39:47,440 --> 00:39:48,280
Why?

661
00:39:48,280 --> 00:39:49,840
Because he's still working on me

662
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:51,560
to make me what I ought to be,

663
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:53,160
and there's still a whole lot of things

664
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:55,140
that I gotta get squared away in my life,

665
00:39:55,140 --> 00:39:56,720
and there's some things, some shortcomings,

666
00:39:56,720 --> 00:39:58,520
some failings in my own life

667
00:39:58,520 --> 00:40:00,420
that I gotta get into the word of God.

668
00:40:00,420 --> 00:40:03,380
And why do I want to judge this brother or this sister

669
00:40:03,380 --> 00:40:05,740
on this thing while they can just turn around

670
00:40:05,740 --> 00:40:07,580
and take the scriptures and just, no, no, no.

671
00:40:07,580 --> 00:40:11,340
We focus, the priority is on doing.

672
00:40:11,340 --> 00:40:14,360
To be doers of the word and not hearers only.

673
00:40:15,220 --> 00:40:17,460
We find that he says at the end of verse number 11,

674
00:40:17,460 --> 00:40:20,540
notice with me again in James four and verse number 11,

675
00:40:20,540 --> 00:40:24,740
but if thou judge the law, thou art not a doer of the law,

676
00:40:24,740 --> 00:40:25,980
but a judge.

677
00:40:26,980 --> 00:40:31,540
The reality is that the one that would rise

678
00:40:31,540 --> 00:40:35,580
to the opportunity, if we could use that word,

679
00:40:35,580 --> 00:40:38,180
to be involved or engaged in judgment

680
00:40:38,180 --> 00:40:40,500
as we see in First Corinthians five and six

681
00:40:40,500 --> 00:40:43,180
and in John seven, would be somebody

682
00:40:43,180 --> 00:40:46,580
that's already a doer of the work.

683
00:40:46,580 --> 00:40:48,580
A doer of the word.

684
00:40:48,580 --> 00:40:52,780
Why was it that certain people were selected by Moses

685
00:40:52,780 --> 00:40:54,920
after Jethro gave the counsel?

686
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:57,240
Why is it that the Lord Jesus Christ

687
00:40:57,240 --> 00:40:58,320
gave certain information?

688
00:40:58,320 --> 00:41:00,840
Why is it that Paul, as he's speaking to the church

689
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:03,840
in Corinth, he's saying, listen, there's not one among you

690
00:41:03,840 --> 00:41:06,280
that can judge between these things.

691
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:07,560
So who would be the one?

692
00:41:07,560 --> 00:41:09,520
How do you determine who the one is?

693
00:41:09,520 --> 00:41:11,700
Well, it's somebody that's not perfect

694
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:13,960
because none of us are, but it's somebody

695
00:41:13,960 --> 00:41:18,960
that faithfully is applying and doing the word of God.

696
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:23,280
And so he says in verse 12, really interesting verse 12,

697
00:41:23,280 --> 00:41:25,640
it says, there is one lawgiver who is able

698
00:41:25,640 --> 00:41:27,280
to save and to destroy.

699
00:41:27,280 --> 00:41:30,360
Who art thou that judgest another?

700
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:32,880
Really, as you look at verse number 12,

701
00:41:32,880 --> 00:41:35,840
there's a truth that we must acknowledge.

702
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:39,040
The truth is this, there's one lawgiver.

703
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:39,880
That's God.

704
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:43,800
And the truth is this, that he is able

705
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:46,720
to save and to destroy.

706
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:52,480
He is the one true lawgiver.

707
00:41:54,520 --> 00:41:56,300
We find that over in the book of Hebrews,

708
00:41:56,300 --> 00:41:57,680
